  prose(<<~'CANONICAL_PROSE', origin: :published)
    ## Overview
    
    ☽'slew Nisaemesius~ is a Nightshelf colony carved into the volcanic substrate of The Berg's deep tunnels, founded during the Clever Ice Age by Crypt-Chancellor Silvcaeclerae-fawn~, who led settlers from Nightfall Shelf — the Nightshelf's principal settlement — into the dark. The colony spirals downward in concentric rings: public caverns lit by bioluminescent fungi and fire-braziers on the upper levels; sacred and administrative spaces descending into genuine darkness where the ice holds older impressions. It was built as a beacon of fire-mining ambition. It remains, at present, a study in what ambition costs.
    
    ## Structure and Succession
    
    The Whispered Shrift~, the colony's first structure and ritual center, sits at its heart. The frost-scarring on its walls — permanent, resistant to all remediation — is the colony's most visible record of institutional failure. Three factions have held the Shrift in succession: Weal' Clique~, who built it under Silvcaeclerae-fawn~'s founding charter; the Cell (owl-sworn), a clandestine faction that claimed authority during the consolidation period; and the doctrinal regime of Iudicium∴culum, which tore the structure open — the chronicles do not specify whether this was literal or figurative, and the ice-memory impressions support both readings.
    
    The current ideological presence is The Way∴ens, an open-knowledge movement centered on two artifacts — The Dreaming Tooth, a resonance artifact of disputed origin, and Xueshei's Compass — which has spread through the lower chambers. The colony's residents describe its influence with characteristic Nightshelf understatement: *the place where we learned to smile while drowning.*
    
    ## The Abys∴uina and Decline
    
    The Abys∴uina — a catastrophic steam eruption in the Lower Galleries — killed what the chronicles report as one thousand penguins in a single event. The round number should give the reader pause; it gives me pause. The fable-chronicle *The City that Grew Fat on Fire* attributes the disaster to Retenusus and his Sun-Shawled followers, whose forbidden memory-burning practice destabilized the deep tunnels. Every ice-crystal patch across the lower rings traces the eruption's path.
    
    The fire-core veins at the sixth depth are now exhausted — not unstable, *finished* — and the structural cracks above the second ring have widened past what ice-crystal patching can address. The deep passages below the Thron∴mbra Fracta threshold were sealed after the last courier route was logged. The encrypted correspondence in *Messages Past the Seventeen*, between Depth-Purveyor ☽'Cilocum and ☽'Otrolal the Watchful, documents the resource shortages and structural anxieties that preceded this closure.
    
    The Thrumed~ Shadow-glass — an obsidian relic veined with captured fire-light — was held here before being stolen by the orca Rend Kzulrora and subsequently changing hands during the Mbra∴silentiu.
    
    ## Present Condition
    
    The colony trades through the adjacent tunnel-settlement of ☽'slew Ravium~. Fire-cores still flow. Orca raiders have been repelled. The Foedus∴sper covenant binds competing guild-masters to shared accountability during the colony's great festival. The locals gather in the lower-warmth caverns for fire-tea and gossip.
    
    The ice beneath the colony holds impressions of what Silvcaeclerae-fawn~ found — and sacrificed — in the deepest tunnels during the founding. Nightshelf proverbs warn against pressing one's flippers to it during the Long Dark. The cracks in the ceiling are widening. No one discusses why.
