  annotation "note_1771589030197_0", anchor: "killed what the chronicles report as one thousand penguins in a single event", text: "Weal' Clique~ administrative tallies produced after the eruption, during a succession crisis in which the Clique had every incentive to magnify catastrophe. The thermal scarring at sixth-depth stratum is consistent with a major steam breach — I am not disputing the event. But the habitation density required for a thousand casualties in the Lower Galleries exceeds every population estimate I have cross-referenced by a factor I find uncomfortable. Four hundred is supportable. Six hundred requires assumptions I cannot make. The round number persists because grief rounds up and no one corrects grief.", type: :skepticism, display: :full
  annotation "note_1771589030197_1", anchor: "Three factions have held the Shrift in succession", text: "And the orca jaw survived all three transitions. Built into the wall by one authority, inherited by two others, removed by none. How extraordinary that this is the one thing they agreed on.", type: :commentary, display: :popout
  annotation "note_1771589030197_2", anchor: "impressions of what Silvcaeclerae-fawn~ found — and sacrificed — in the deepest tunnels during the founding", text: "Deliberately vague in the main text because the alternative is specificity I cannot adequately source. What the deep ice holds at those strata predates Silvcaeclerae-fawn~. It predates any penguin. I have catalogued comparable impressions in the Foundation Depths — movement recorded in ice so old it has no business recording anything, patterns that do not correspond to any species in the archive. That Silvcaeclerae-fawn~ encountered something at founding-depth is documented. That she understood what she encountered is the charitable reading. The Nightshelf proverb about pressing one's flippers to the ice during the Long Dark is not superstition. It is engineering advice.", type: :commentary, display: :full
